<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27233" root="طهو and طهى" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَهْىٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طُهًى</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>Thin clouds.</i> (TA.)
[See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَهَآءٌ</span>.] ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  And it is said in the “ Nawádir ” that <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَمِعْتُ طَهْيَهُمٌ</span>, as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَغْيَهُمْ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَغْيَهُمْ</span>, means <i>I heard their sound,</i> or <i>voice:</i> [or
<i>their sounds,</i> or <i>voices:</i>] and one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فلان فى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طهى ونهى</span> [app. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فى طَهْىٍ وَنَهْىِ</span>, as though meaning <i>Such a one is engaged in clamour and prohibition</i>]. (TA.)

